The current implementation of podio datamodels does not provide a built-in way to iterate over all defined data and link types in a generated datamodel. When creating algorithms that need to handle every collection type dynamically (e.g., a CollectionMerger that maps collection type names to merge functions), users must maintain a manual mapping of type names to functions. This manual mapping becomes brittle and requires modification whenever the underlying datamodel changes.

Implement functionality in the generated `datamodel.h` file (e.g., `edm4hep.h` for EDM4hep) that exposes a list of all data types and link types defined in the datamodel.

Specifically:
1. Generate a variadic template struct (e.g., `datamodelTypes<T...>`) in the main datamodel header that contains all the collection types as template arguments.
2. Expose this struct so that users can utilize it to automatically iterate over all types.

This allows users to write generic code such as:
```cpp
template <typename T>
void addToMap() {
  m_map[T::typeName] = &CollectionMerger::mergeCollections<T>;
}

template <typename... T>
void addToMapAll(edm4hep::edm4hepDataTypes<T...>&&) {
  (addToMap<T>(), ...);
}

// Usage
#include "edm4hep/edm4hep.h"
struct CollectionMerger {
  std::map<std::string, MergeFunction> m_map;
  CollectionMerger() {
    addToMapAll(edm4hep::edm4hepDataTypes{});
  }
};
```

The implementation should ensure that the generated type lists include all data collection types and link types defined in the datamodel schema, enabling runtime polymorphism without hardcoding type names.

